NOTICE
======

This repository bundles agent skills from more than one source; skills live
under skills/, one directory per skill. Retired skills are kept under
archive/skills/ and are described at the end of this file. Attribution and
licensing, by skill:

Each skill directory carries copies of the license texts that apply to it:
LICENSE in every skill, and each root LICENSE-* file whose source the skill
adapts. A single-skill install (install.py --copy --skill, or a third-party
installer) therefore keeps the notice the MIT license requires. The root files
are canonical, and build/check_provenance.py checks that every copy is
byte-identical to its root file.

Files under runtimes/ are mechanically generated format adapters for the
canonical agents/*.md and commands/*.md sources. They reproduce the source
instruction bodies without changing their provenance or license; each adapter
inherits the attribution and license of its canonical source. The adapter
generator, installer, runtime entrypoint files, and compatibility documentation
are original works by Lowell Mason under this repository's MIT license.

