Archived skills
---------------

archive/skills/ keeps retired skills whole so that one can be restored;
archive/README.md gives the steps. install.py does not install them, no suite
runs their tests, and the skill lints skip them. They were archived on
2026-10-27. All three are Lowell Mason's original works under this
repository's MIT license, and each keeps its LICENSE copy:

    bls-data-context/   (including its ten BLS references: nine program
                        references plus the cross-program ingest reference)
    classification-codes/
    geographic-codes/

classification-codes/ and geographic-codes/ are original works by Lowell
Mason (MIT) whose bundled data/ tables are derived from U.S. Census Bureau,
U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, and Office of Management and Budget
publications (NAICS and SOC structure and concordance workbooks; the Census
occupation code lists; the county gazetteer; the "List 1" CBSA delineation
workbooks). Those publications are
works of the United States Government and are in the public domain under
17 U.S.C. § 105. Each skill's scripts/build.py downloads the exact source
bytes into sources/ (kept verbatim as the audit copy, with URL, sha256, and
retrieval time in MANIFEST.md) and derives data/ from them; the parsing
code, the seed tables, the hand-curated county change log, and all prose
are Lowell Mason's own work. geographic-codes' seeds/county_changes.csv
was verified row by row against the Census Bureau's "Substantial Changes
to Counties and County Equivalent Entities" pages and, for Connecticut,
87 FR 34235; the OMB bulletin dates were read from the bulletins
themselves (13-01, 15-01, 17-01, 18-03, 18-04, 20-01, 23-01).
